From a2edf94539598f1599bb9f12d3b4d1e55c19498b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:28:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 2/5] power: supply: add Silicon Mitus SM5714 fuel gauge
 driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SM5714 is a combo PMIC integrating a charger, a fuel gauge and a
Type-C/USB block. Add a driver for its fuel gauge block, found on Samsung
phones such as the Galaxy A52 (SM7125). It reports battery voltage,
current, temperature and state of charge, read from an indirectly
addressed SRAM.

Based on the downstream SM5714 fuel-gauge driver by map220v, ported to the
current power_supply and probe APIs and cleaned up for upstream. No public
datasheet is available; the register layout and the fixed-point scaling
come from the Samsung downstream driver and were verified against raw
register reads on a Galaxy A52.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
